boethius-1.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: A5: "counted in the sum of thy possessions" is taken as counts as a good or asset to thee (a ruinous burden adds nothing of worth) in A5 and as belongs to thee as thine own (another's virtue is not thine) where servants_thine is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S3) does not follow (boethius-1.logic.r1.sense1)
boethius-1.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S3): possessions_thine = T, servants_burden = T, servants_honest = F, servants_thine = T, servants_thine_2 = F, servants_vicious = T, virtue_others = F
